{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"undivined-rebel-angora","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Symptom\n\nGerrit change 1416 (ticket fd30) earned `LLM-Review +1` but `Verified -1`. The failing step was\n`Git version floor gate` in `build-and-test / pytest`, with:\n\n    ##[error]missing .github/git-version-floor.txt (the single source of the Git version floor)\n\nThe change touched only `Makefile`, `docs/local-dev-env.md` and `docs/user-guide.md` -- nothing\nrelated to git versions.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`.github/git-version-floor.txt` was introduced by ticket 980d ('declare and enforce the Git 2.38+\nfloor'). The Gerrit Verified lane takes the workflow **definition** from the target branch (main,\nwhich now has the gate) but checks out the **change's tree** (which predates the file). So the gate\nruns against a tree that cannot contain its own input.\n\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` already documents this exact hazard and its remedy under\nticket ee2a -- the 'Definition-vs-tree skew guard': a new gate step that consumes a repo file must\nskip, with a log line, when that file is absent from the checked-out tree, then re-enforce on rebase\nand on every post-merge change. The `raw-git-write` gate implements it. The Git version floor gate\ndoes not.\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery open change whose base predates 980d gets a spurious `Verified -1` and must rebase, even when\nits diff is unrelated. This is noise that trains agents and humans to treat `Verified -1` as\n'probably just rebase', which erodes the value of the gate.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nWrap the floor gate's step in the same if-present guard the raw-git-write gate uses: when\n`.github/git-version-floor.txt` is not in the checked-out tree, echo a skip line and pass.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The Git version floor gate skips (with a log line) when `.github/git-version-floor.txt` is\n      absent from the checked-out tree, and enforces normally when present.\n- [ ] A change based before 980d no longer earns `Verified -1` for this reason.\n- [ ] A survey of other gate steps added since ee2a confirms each either consumes no repo file or\n      carries the guard.","id":"58b6-6af1-f975-4820","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Git version floor gate lacks the ee2a if-present guard, so it fails every change based before 980d"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785908868692812001,"uuid":"816b60d9-19ef-42b7-b31d-91395d04c74b"}